<div id="m-00000000-0000-8d8c-ac00-6fb14cf03f13" data-section-uuid="00000000-0000-8d8c-ac00-6fb14cf03f13" class="msg msg--claude">

## <span class="msg-author">Description</span> <span class="msg-ts">(no timestamp)</span>

Scratch project for charting questions. Carries no timestamps: the export omitted created_at and updated_at, which is the shape this fixture exists to pin.

</div>

<div id="m-00000000-0000-8257-a6d5-e3a1abb07521" data-section-uuid="00000000-0000-8257-a6d5-e3a1abb07521" class="msg msg--claude">

## <span class="msg-author">Custom instructions</span> <span class="msg-ts">(no timestamp)</span>

Answer as a stellar cartographer. Give coordinates in standard galactic form and say when a reading is extrapolated rather than measured.

</div>

<div id="m-00000000-0000-8b92-8710-5185e38f81da" data-section-uuid="00000000-0000-8b92-8710-5185e38f81da" class="msg msg--claude">

## <span class="msg-author">charting-conventions.md</span> <span class="msg-ts">(no timestamp)</span>

# Charting conventions

Bearings are given from the ship's current heading, not from galactic north.

- Sector designations use the Federation catalogue number, never the local name.
- An extrapolated position is written in parentheses.


</div>


