<h1 class="page-title" data-page-title-uuid="00000000-0000-8731-b6c5-2d66a2c4265c">Warp Field Recalibration <a class="source-link" href="https://claude.ai/chat/c0000007-1701-4d00-8000-00000000c007" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">↗</a></h1>

<div id="m-0b75c9a3-4680-8f18-9b74-f1de68268d1d" data-section-uuid="0b75c9a3-4680-8f18-9b74-f1de68268d1d" class="msg msg--claude">

## <span class="msg-author">Human</span> <time class="msg-ts" datetime="2369-04-18T09:00:00+00:00" title="2369-04-18 09:00:00 UTC">Fri Apr 18th, 2369 at 09:00</time>

Geordi, how far can we push the warp field before the nacelles complain?

</div>

<details class="tool-group">
<summary>🛠 2 tool steps</summary>

<div id="m-0b75c9a3-5a08-8fec-97d8-d163ce521717" data-section-uuid="0b75c9a3-5a08-8fec-97d8-d163ce521717" class="msg msg--claude">

## <span class="msg-author">claude-opus-4-7</span> <time class="msg-ts" datetime="2369-04-18T09:00:05+00:00" title="2369-04-18 09:00:05 UTC">Fri Apr 18th, 2369 at 09:00</time>

<details><summary>Tool use: web_search — Searching the web</summary>

```json
{
  "query": "Galaxy class maximum sustainable warp"
}
```
</details>

</div>

<div id="m-0b75c9a3-65c0-88ab-a3e5-89b60c21f729" data-section-uuid="0b75c9a3-65c0-88ab-a3e5-89b60c21f729" class="msg msg--claude">

## <span class="msg-author">claude-opus-4-7</span> <time class="msg-ts" datetime="2369-04-18T09:00:08+00:00" title="2369-04-18 09:00:08 UTC">Fri Apr 18th, 2369 at 09:00</time>

<details><summary>Tool result: web_search</summary>

- [Warp factor](https://memory-alpha.test/wiki/Warp_factor) — Memory Alpha
- [Galaxy class propulsion](https://tech-manual.test/ncc-1701-d/propulsion) — Starfleet Technical Manual

</details>

</div>

</details>

<div id="m-0b75c9a3-94a0-89c6-b27b-e588f8d0b997" data-section-uuid="0b75c9a3-94a0-89c6-b27b-e588f8d0b997" class="msg msg--claude">

## <span class="msg-author">claude-opus-4-7</span> <time class="msg-ts" datetime="2369-04-18T09:00:20+00:00" title="2369-04-18 09:00:20 UTC">Fri Apr 18th, 2369 at 09:00</time>

Sustained warp 9.2 is the rated ceiling; the nacelles tolerate 9.6 for about twelve hours before the coils need a full recalibration.

**Sources**

1. [Warp factor](https://memory-alpha.test/wiki/Warp_factor) — Memory Alpha
2. [Galaxy class propulsion](https://tech-manual.test/ncc-1701-d/propulsion) — Starfleet Technical Manual
3. [Warp coil](https://memory-alpha.test/wiki/Warp_coil) — Memory Alpha

</div>

<details class="branch">
<summary>✎ Another version · 2 messages</summary>

<div id="m-0b75c9a4-30e0-8bd1-a2ad-d47516561b38" data-section-uuid="0b75c9a4-30e0-8bd1-a2ad-d47516561b38" class="msg msg--claude">

## <span class="msg-author">Human</span> <time class="msg-ts" datetime="2369-04-18T09:01:00+00:00" title="2369-04-18 09:01:00 UTC">Fri Apr 18th, 2369 at 09:01</time>

Give me the coil efficiencies as a table.

</div>

<div id="m-0b75c9a4-57f0-882c-9555-81a83be27d89" data-section-uuid="0b75c9a4-57f0-882c-9555-81a83be27d89" class="msg msg--claude">

